5.3 Workflow completeness

A feature is complete only when its interface, business logic, validation, persistence, authorization, error handling, and relevant tests work together to the required degree.

Do not represent an inert button, hard-coded table, client-only form, or local demonstration state as a completed institutional workflow.

If a module is only partially implemented, label it accurately.

